---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const upworkUrl = 'https://www.upwork.com/services/product/writing-translation-professional-sops-and-clear-process-documentation-2098097452881572813?ref=project_share';
---
<BaseLayout title="Process Improvement & Business Operations" current="/process-improvement/" description="Process improvement, SOP program leadership, reporting, quality control, workflow improvement, documentation, and selected project services from Richard Allen.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Process Improvement & Business Operations</div><h1>Turn scattered work into repeatable, usable systems.</h1><p class="lede">I’m strongest when a process needs to be documented, simplified, coordinated, measured, standardized, governed, or translated into something people can actually use.</p></div></section>

<section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="callout"><strong>Selected proof point:</strong> led a year-long Oregon Employment Department SOP project and project team that created 100 new SOPs and corrected or standardized 25+ legacy SOPs.</div>
  <div class="process-flow" aria-label="Process improvement approach">
    <div class="flow-step"><span>1</span><strong>Understand</strong><small>How the work actually happens</small></div>
    <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
    <div class="flow-step"><span>2</span><strong>Organize</strong><small>People, steps, inputs, and decisions</small></div>
    <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
    <div class="flow-step"><span>3</span><strong>Document</strong><small>Clear instructions people can follow</small></div>
    <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
    <div class="flow-step"><span>4</span><strong>Govern & improve</strong><small>Keep the system useful over time</small></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">SOP</div><h3>SOP program leadership</h3><p>Created 100 new SOPs, corrected and standardized 25+ legacy SOPs, established standards, reviewed and accepted completed work, coached contributors, built the centralized repository, and established ongoing creation and maintenance guidelines.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">QA</div><h3>Quality & process control</h3><p>At HawkSoft, investigated an employee-quality issue involving call and voicemail handling, identified multiple representatives using the workaround, coached through an action plan, and helped revise QA policy so calls of any length could be reviewed.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">KPI</div><h3>Reporting for better decisions</h3><p>Built recurring management reporting from raw support and call data, analyzed trends, and made recommendations on staffing, training, procedures, policies/processes, and future needs; Richard later presented most of this reporting directly to directors/upper management.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">400+</div><h3>Workforce reporting at scale</h3><p>At Oregon Health Authority, managed 400+ position records and maintained 20+ recurring and ad-hoc workforce reports while coordinating with Recruiting, HR, Classification & Compensation, Budget, DEI, and leadership.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">↻</div><h3>Change & release support</h3><p>Led staff readiness for a major HawkSoft accounting-software redesign through six months of advance communication, biweekly developer/staff education during the final two months, extra go-live support, and continued training afterward.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">CX</div><h3>Customer experience systems</h3><p>At The Kotter Group, established and managed a Customer Experience / Customer Success function, gathered customer feedback across the client base, resolved issues, created training and release documentation, and supported software functional testing and enablement.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">AUD</div><h3>Accuracy in changing environments</h3><p>Audited hundreds of Pandemic Unemployment Assistance applications while guidance changed rapidly, using tracking and research tools and creating training/onboarding and operational tracking materials.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">20</div><h3>Supply & warehouse operations</h3><p>At Aramark Foodservice, typically supervised about 20 people across warehouse staff, drivers, and inmate workers while handling procurement/supply management and more than $1 million in inventory annually.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section project-services"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Available for selected project work</div><h2>SOP & process documentation</h2></div><p class="section-note">A secondary project-work pathway alongside my primary full-time search.</p></div>
  <div class="project-service-panel">
    <div>
      <p class="project-service-lede">If an important process is undocumented, inconsistent, outdated, or mostly living in someone’s head, I can help turn it into clear instructions your team can actually use.</p>
      <div class="service-grid">
        <div><strong>Standard Operating Procedures</strong><span>New SOPs built from notes, screenshots, forms, interviews, or existing materials.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Workflow Documentation</strong><span>Who does what, when, with which inputs, decisions, systems, and handoffs.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Training & Onboarding Guides</strong><span>Practical documentation that helps people learn and repeat the work consistently.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Existing SOP Cleanup</strong><span>Improve clarity, consistency, organization, usability, and missing or confusing steps.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Support-Operations Procedures</strong><span>Escalation, service, troubleshooting, quality, and support-process documentation.</span></div>
        <div><strong>Documentation Governance</strong><span>Standards, review practices, repositories, and maintenance guidelines.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="project-proof">
      <div class="eyebrow">Why this work fits</div>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Year-long SOP program: 100 new SOPs + 25+ legacy corrections</li>
        <li>Centralized repository, standards, review/acceptance, and maintenance governance</li>
        <li>Dozens of historical HawkSoft sales policies/procedures documented</li>
        <li>Kotter product, training, usage, release, and customer-education documentation</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/project-work/">View project services</a><a class="button secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href={upworkUrl}>View Upwork SOP service</a></div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
